@startuml zipper-cursor
' ============================================================================
' zipper-cursor.puml — the dual-cursor "synchronize-and-emit" state machine
' that drives a binary set-algebra combinator (intersection shown).
'
' A combinator keeps one operand cursor per dictionary (left L, right R). It
' advances them IN LOCKSTEP: every `descend(label)` / `children()` is forwarded
' to BOTH cursors over the SAME label, so they always sit at the same path. The
' EMIT decision is the only place the combinators differ — it is the predicate
' over (L.is_final, R.is_final):
'     INTERSECTION  : emit iff  L_final AND R_final
'     UNION         : emit iff  L_final OR  R_final
'     DIFFERENCE    : emit iff  L_final AND NOT R_final
'     SYM-DIFFERENCE: emit iff  exactly one final
'     VALUE-DIFF    : emit iff  L_final AND R_final AND L.value != R.value
' This diagram traces the iterator's DFS: descend a shared child, test the emit
' predicate, then ascend (pop) and try the next sibling. INTERSECTION's
' `descend` also PRUNES — if either cursor cannot take the label, the whole
' subtree is skipped (no point descending where the sets cannot agree).
' Source of truth: src/intersection_zipper.rs (descend / children / is_final /
' IntersectionIterator::next); the emit predicates above per combinator file.
'
' Color key:
'   green  (#C8E6C9) = both cursors live & aligned (the productive state)
'   amber  (#FFF59D) = synchronize / advance work (descend · sibling · ascend)
'   blue   (#BBDEFB) = EMIT — a term is yielded to the consumer
'   grey   (#ECEFF1 / #37474F) = prune / exhausted / borders / transitions
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontName "DejaVu Sans"
  AttributeFontName "DejaVu Sans"
}

title Dual-cursor advance — intersection synchronizes L and R, emits only where BOTH agree

[*] --> Aligned : new(vec![L, R])\nboth cursors at root, path = []

state "Aligned\nL and R sit at the SAME path\n(both Some — operands still agree)" as Aligned #C8E6C9

state "TestEmit\nevaluate the combinator predicate\nINTERSECTION: L.is_final() && R.is_final()" as TestEmit #FFF59D

state "Emit\nyield (path, zipper) to consumer\nvalue = strategy.merge(L.value, R.value)" as Emit #BBDEFB

state "Descend\nlabel ∈ children(L) ∩ children(R)\ndescend(label) on BOTH cursors" as Descend #FFF59D

state "Sibling / Ascend\npop DFS frame · advance to next\nshared child of the parent" as Ascend #FFF59D

state "Prune\nL or R cannot take label →\nsubtree cannot intersect: SKIP" as Prune #ECEFF1

state "Exhausted\nDFS stack empty —\nno more aligned children" as Done #ECEFF1

Aligned --> TestEmit : visit node

TestEmit -[#1565C0,thickness=2]-> Emit : predicate TRUE\n(both final)
TestEmit --> Descend : predicate FALSE\n(continue traversal)
Emit -[#1565C0]-> Descend : after yield,\nkeep traversing subtree

Descend -[#2E7D32,thickness=2]-> Aligned : both descended\n(label in BOTH) → realign
Descend -[#C62828,dashed]-> Prune : label missing in L or R
Prune --> Ascend : drop subtree

Aligned --> Ascend : no more children here
Ascend --> Aligned : next sibling exists\n(re-descend shared label)
Ascend --> Done : DFS stack empty

Done --> [*]

note right of Descend
  LOCKSTEP rule: a label is followed only if it is
  present in BOTH cursors' children (set ∩). UNION
  follows a label present in EITHER (set ∪) and never
  takes the Prune edge — it keeps a cursor as `None`
  where that operand lacks the path.
end note

note right of Emit
  Only the EMIT predicate changes per combinator;
  the descend / ascend / sibling machinery is shared.
  DIFFERENCE follows LEFT's children (right tags along
  for the exclusion test); INTERSECTION & VALUE-DIFF
  follow the ∩; UNION & SYM-DIFFERENCE follow the ∪.
end note
@enduml
